{"raw": {"https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Access-Services-Librarian---Faculty_R-097876": {"title": "Assistant Librarian, Access Services", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Librarian, Access Services Agency Texas A&M University - Central Texas Department Library Services Proposed Minimum Salary $4,839.42 monthly Job Location Killeen, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Access Services Librarian will coordinate daily circulation services, including tracking course reserves, documenting user borrowing standards, and facilitating collection access for onsite and digital users. Additional duties will include individualized instruction at the reference desk, service through academic or library committees, and adherence to faculty librarian scholarship standards. The librarian may oversee a small number of part-time staff or student worker direct reports and complete basic administrative tasks. A Presidential Proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on all new H\u20111B petitions filed after September 21, 2025, and Texas A&M University\u2013Central Texas will not pay this fee. Additionally, a moratorium issued by Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026, restricts the filing of new H\u20111B petitions unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. Applicants must be authorized to work for any U.S. employer. Responsibilities : Manage to 2-4 part-time employees in access services. Create access services schedules for the Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Provide training for circulation services, including item lending, lamination, comb binding, printing, scanning, and other related tasks. Develop access services policies and procedures. Maintain collection statistics for common access services, such as annual lending, gate counts, and request types. Maintain circulation policy and permission settings in the Alma LMS. Staff the reference desk for 8 to 12 hours per week, split across two or more shifts, including one weekday evening. Develop collections in assigned subject fields that could include biology, chemistry, criminal justice, sociology, business, or other areas, depending on skill set and in partnership with faculty. Manage and coordinate library displays. Assist with library outreach and marketing, as needed, to help the department connect with campus and community members. Events may take place on or off campus. Assist with library instruction or public service events, as needed. Faculty Research and Service: Serves as a member of committees in the library and the university.\u00a0 Remains current in the library discipline and assigned liaison areas. Publishes chapters, book reviews, or other peer-reviewed written content for theoretical or practical aspects of the library field. Participates in conferences and professional organizations. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to multitask and work cooperatively with others. Ability to design a variety of online and in-person general and subject-specific instruction sessions. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Effective interpersonal and customer service skills. Strong critical thinking, problem-solving, organizational, and decision-making skills.\u00a0 \u00a0 Minimum Qualifications A Master of Library Science (MLS) degree, Master of Library and Information Science (MLIS) degree, or another equivalent from an American Library Association (ALA)-accredited university or college. Must be self-motivated, creative, and innovative with excellent interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications Second master\u2019s degree, with a preference for the hard sciences, computer science, social sciences, or business. A bachelor\u2019s degree in the hard sciences, computer science, social sciences, or business. Two years of experience in a library, with a preference for academic libraries. Experience working in access services or an adjacent role at a library, with more weight given for two or more years of access services experience. \u00a0 Experience managing employees, especially student workers or part-time library employees. More weight will be given for management in the context of access services. Experience providing library instruction. Experience working in reference at an academic library. Experience managing circulation policy and permission settings in the library's ILS (Alma) or a similar ILS. \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Salary: $ 58,073.00 Hours: Monday, Tuesday, Thursday, and Friday from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.; Wednesday from 12:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. Supervision of Others: This position may supervise other employees. Work Location: This is not a remote position. The selected candidate will be required to work on campus. \u00a0 To Apply: Please apply directly on our Texas A&M University-Central Texas Job Site . Applicants should submit a cover letter, r\u00e9sum\u00e9, and contact information for three professional references. Transcripts should be uploaded in the attachment section of the application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Management-Strategy_R-097888-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Management/Strategy", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Management/Strategy Agency Texas A&M University - Central Texas Department College of Business Administration Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Killeen, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Business Administration (COBA) at Texas A&M University-Central Texas welcomes highly qualified applicants to fill an immediate need for an Assistant or Associate Professor in Management / Strategy starting in Fall 2027. This is a tenure-track faculty position. Application reviews will begin immediately. We are looking for a dynamic and collegial teacher-scholar with a passion for teaching and a multi-faceted track record of excellence both within and beyond the classroom. Our greatest and immediate teaching need is for our undergraduate business strategy capstone course. Our hope is that this faculty member will deliver our capstone strategy course in such a way that students complete their undergraduate business programs on a high note. Courses in other related areas may also be available on a limited basis depending on applicant qualifications and interest. About Texas A&M University \u2013 Central Texas Established as an independent member of the Texas A&M University System in 2009, A&M-Central Texas is a friendly and dynamic regional teaching institution that prides itself on excellence in instruction, but also embraces a growing emphasis on research.\u00a0 A&M-Central Texas is truly unique in that it is an upper- and masters-level institution, offering only junior- and senior-level coursework needed to successfully complete baccalaureate degrees and all coursework leading to the completion of master\u2019s degrees.\u00a0 As such, A&M-Central Texas maintains active partnerships with the major community colleges within the Austin and Central Texas region, as well with Fort Hood, a premier outpost of the U.S. Army and one of the largest military installations in the world.\u00a0 Our multifaceted student demographic includes a significant proportion of first-generation college students, non-traditional learners, and military-affiliated personnel.\u00a0 \u00a0 The College of Business Administration is accredited by AACSB, and we are eager to have dynamic and collegial new faculty members partner with us in pursuit of our major strategic initiatives, of which there are many on the near horizon (most notably, a DBA program anticipated to launch Fall 2027 pending SACSCOC final approval).\u00a0 This is an exciting time of rapid change within the College that affords new faculty members many opportunities to make an immediate, significant, and lasting impact. \u00a0 A&M-Central Texas is located on the southern edge of Killeen, TX, a city of approximately 150,000 located about halfway between Austin and Waco\u2014about 60 miles either way.\u00a0 Our faculty members enjoy a wide variety of living options by virtue of the culture in the area\u2014from quiet and rural to bustling and cosmopolitan.\u00a0 It is an easy drive to great art, food, shopping, and night life as well as to hunting, fishing, hiking, and camping for those who prefer the outdoors.\u00a0 Central Texas is also a great place for families, with many options for schooling, worship, civic engagement, and recreation.\u00a0 It also has light traffic and a reasonable cost of living.\u00a0 The major metropolitan areas of Houston, Dallas-Fort Worth, and San Antonio are all within a 3-hour radius of Killeen.\u00a0 \u00a0 Responsibilities The candidate will be expected to provide quality, engaging instruction for typically three courses of undergraduate business strategy per term, primarily at the undergraduate level and in a variety of course delivery formats (face-to-face, online, or hybrid), with fully online being the most in-demand option at present.\u00a0 Summer teaching opportunities may also available as dictated by student demand and department needs.\u00a0 \u00a0 Some scholarly contributions are also required.\u00a0 The candidate is expected have sufficient scholarly and/or professional activities to have \u201cscholarly academic\u201d status upon arrival per AACSB faculty classifications, and to have a healthy pipeline of works in progress, where health is measured more by viability and impact than by volume.\u00a0 Scholarship is but one category of currency and impact with which faculty may engage: others include maintaining a recognized professional certification, presenting at academic conferences, engaging in consulting or other industry-related activities, and completing other relevant professional training and development activities.\u00a0 Professional development funds are available to support all of these endeavors, and faculty within the College frequently collaborate on research projects together.\u00a0 \u00a0 In regard to service, faculty are expected to support the department, college, and university with committee work, but first-year faculty are exempt from this.\u00a0 In addition, faculty are expected to have some sort of service to their profession and/or to the community, but again, service contribution impact and quality are more important than the numbers of activities engaged in. \u00a0Faculty generally have a lot of discretion in determining how best they can add value through their various service activities.\u00a0 A Presidential Proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on all new H\u20111B petitions filed after September 21, 2025, and Texas A&M University\u2013Central Texas will not pay this fee. Additionally, a moratorium issued by Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026, restricts the filing of new H\u20111B petitions unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. Applicants must be authorized to work for any U.S. employer. Minimum Qualifications: To be eligible to apply for this position, candidates should: Possess a terminal degree (doctorate) in strategic management or a closely-related discipline from a regionally accredited university Be eligible for the AACSB \u201cscholarly academic\u201d faculty classification Have a documented track record of successfully teaching business strategy, including in fully online formats \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: The ideal candidate for this position would also possess: At least three (3) years of full-time collegiate teaching experience Experience working with doctoral students Industry experience, including ongoing connections Proficiency in creating original, dynamic, and engaging online course instructional materials Great administrative, organizational, and interpersonal skills to support successful instruction to a largely non-traditional, first-generation, and military-affiliated student body \u00a0 \u00a0 Salary: Commensurate Hours: Faculty hours; M-F; hours may vary by assignment and course modality. To Apply: Please apply directly on our Texas A&M University-Central Texas Job Site . Applicants are required to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), and either the contact information for three professional references or three letters of recommendation. Additional materials, such as a teaching philosophy statement and transcripts, are optional but strongly encouraged. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Adjunct-Faculty---Marriage---Family-Therapy_R-083523-1": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Marriage & Family Therapy", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Faculty - Marriage & Family Therapy Agency Texas A&M University - Central Texas Department College Of Education and Human Development Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Killeen, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Applications for part-time adjunct faculty positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed when openings become available. Future teaching assignments are on a semester-by-semester basis, which may include fall, spring and summer.\u00a0 The Marriage and Family Therapy Program within the Department of Counseling and Psychology at Texas A&M University \u2013 Central Texas is seeking applicants for adjunct instructors. The successful candidate(s) will be expected to teach graduate course either in person or online in the marriage and family therapy program. Experience and enthusiasm for teaching and working with graduate students is essential. A Ph.D. in Marriage and Family Therapy or related field is required. Applicants must also have a clear MFT identity (e.g. membership in professional associations, research, presentations, clinical practice) Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, graduate transcripts, and three professional letters of reference. Primarily responsible for the teaching/learning process. Adjunct instructors are hired to teach on a temporary and part-time basis. Adjunct instructors teaching courses for credit must meet the same requirements for professional and scholarly preparation as their full-time counterparts teaching in the same discipline. Disclosure: A Presidential Proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on all new H\u20111B petitions filed after September 21, 2025, and Texas A&M University\u2013Central Texas will not pay this fee. Additionally, a moratorium issued by Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026, restricts the filing of new H\u20111B petitions unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. Applicants must be authorized to work for any U.S. employer. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Experience in clinical practice or instruction related to marriage and family therapy Exhibit enthusiasm for graduate teaching and employing innovative teaching methods. Minimum Qualifications : Ph.D. in Marriage and Family Therapy or related field Preferred Qualifications: MFT Doctoral Degree from COAMFTE accredited program AAMFT clinical membership and Approved Supervisor designation. To Apply: Please apply directly on our Texas A&M University-Central Texas Job Site . Applicants are required to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), graduate transcripts, and either the contact information for three professional references or three letters of recommendation. Completed employment application material must include: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Graduate Transcripts At least 3 Professional references or letters of reference All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Management-Leadership_R-097771": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Management/Leadership", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Management/Leadership Agency Texas A&M University - Central Texas Department College of Business Administration Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Killeen, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Business Administration (COBA) at Texas A&M University-Central Texas welcomes highly qualified applicants to fill an immediate need for an Assistant Professor in Management / Leadership starting in Fall 2027.\u00a0 This is a tenure-track faculty position.\u00a0 Application reviews will begin immediately.\u00a0 We are looking for a dynamic and collegial teacher-scholar with a passion for teaching and a multi-faceted track record of excellence both within and beyond the classroom.\u00a0 This faculty member would be expected to teach leadership-related courses at a variety of levels and in a variety of modalities.\u00a0 Assigned courses will include undergraduate leadership and one or more of the following graduate courses: organization development and change (masters), cross-sector partnerships (masters), global leadership theory and practice (masters), leadership formation and development (masters), and any one of the in-development doctoral courses that would support our DBA leadership emphasis area (still pending final SACSCOC approval). \u00a0Other courses may also be available on a limited basis depending on applicant qualifications and interest.\u00a0 \u00a0 While this position is being advertised at the rank of Assistant Professor, we warmly welcome applications from candidates with distinguished records and broader experience. \u00a0Depending on institutional needs and individual qualifications, consideration may be given for credit toward years of service and/or appointment at the rank of Associate Professor. \u00a0Please note that tenure upon hire is possible but atypical and is determined on a case-by-case basis in consultation with the Provost. \u00a0 About Texas A&M University \u2013 Central Texas Established as an independent member of the Texas A&M University System in 2009, A&M-Central Texas is a friendly and dynamic regional teaching institution that prides itself on excellence in instruction, but also embraces a growing emphasis on research.\u00a0 A&M-Central Texas is truly unique in that it is an upper- and masters-level institution, offering only junior- and senior-level coursework needed to successfully complete baccalaureate degrees and all coursework leading to the completion of master\u2019s degrees.\u00a0 As such, A&M-Central Texas maintains active partnerships with the major community colleges within the Austin and Central Texas region, as well with Fort Hood, a premier outpost of the U.S. Army and one of the largest military installations in the world.\u00a0 Our multifaceted student demographic includes a significant proportion of first-generation college students, non-traditional learners, and military-affiliated personnel.\u00a0 \u00a0 The College of Business Administration is accredited by AACSB, and we are eager to have dynamic and collegial new faculty members partner with us in pursuit of our major strategic initiatives, of which there are many on the near horizon (most notably, a DBA program anticipated to launch Fall 2027 pending SACSCOC final approval).\u00a0 This is an exciting time of rapid change within the College that affords new faculty members many opportunities to make an immediate, significant, and lasting impact. \u00a0 A&M-Central Texas is located on the southern edge of Killeen, TX, a city of approximately 150,000 located about halfway between Austin and Waco\u2014about 60 miles either way.\u00a0 Our faculty members enjoy a wide variety of living options by virtue of the culture in the area\u2014from quiet and rural to bustling and cosmopolitan.\u00a0 It is an easy drive to great art, food, shopping, and night life as well as to hunting, fishing, hiking, and camping for those who prefer the outdoors.\u00a0 Central Texas is also a great place for families, with many options for schooling, worship, civic engagement, and recreation.\u00a0 It also has light traffic and a reasonable cost of living.\u00a0 The major metropolitan areas of Houston, Dallas-Fort Worth, and San Antonio are all within a 3-hour radius of Killeen.\u00a0 \u00a0 Responsibilities The candidate will be expected to provide quality, engaging instruction for typically three courses per long term in a variety of course delivery formats (face-to-face, online, or hybrid), with fully online being the most in-demand option at present.\u00a0 Summer teaching opportunities may also available as dictated by student demand and department needs.\u00a0 Some scholarly contributions are also required.\u00a0 The candidate is expected have sufficient scholarly and/or professional activities to have \u201cscholarly academic\u201d status upon arrival per AACSB faculty classifications, and to have a healthy pipeline of works in progress, where health is measured more by viability and impact than by volume.\u00a0 Scholarship is but one category of currency and impact with which faculty may engage: others include maintaining a recognized professional certification, presenting at academic conferences, engaging in consulting or other industry-related activities, and completing other relevant professional training and development activities.\u00a0 Professional development funds are available to support all of these endeavors, and faculty within the College frequently collaborate on research projects together.\u00a0 \u00a0 In regard to service, faculty are expected to support the department, college, and university with committee work, but first-year faculty are exempt from this.\u00a0 In addition, faculty are expected to have some sort of service to their profession and/or to the community, but again, service contribution impact and quality are more important than the number of activities engaged in. \u00a0Faculty (in consultation with the department chair) generally have a lot of discretion in determining how best they can add value through their various service activities.\u00a0 A Presidential Proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on all new H\u20111B petitions filed after September 21, 2025, and Texas A&M University\u2013Central Texas will not pay this fee. Additionally, a moratorium issued by Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026, restricts the filing of new H\u20111B petitions unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. Applicants must be authorized to work for any U.S. employer. \u00a0 Minimum Qualifications: To be eligible to apply for this position, candidates should: Possess a terminal degree (doctorate) in management / leadership or a closely-related discipline from a regionally accredited university Be eligible for the AACSB \u201cscholarly academic\u201d faculty classification Have a documented track record of successfully teaching leadership courses, including in fully online formats \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: The ideal candidate for this position would also possess: At least three (3) years of full-time collegiate teaching experience Experience working with doctoral students Industry experience, including ongoing connections Proficiency in creating original, dynamic, and engaging online course instructional materials Great administrative, organizational, and interpersonal skills to support successful instruction to a largely non-traditional, first-generation, and military-affiliated student body Salary: Commensurate Hours: Faculty hours; M-F; hours may vary by assignment and course modality. To Apply: Please apply directly on our Texas A&M University-Central Texas Job Site . Applicants are required to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), and either the contact information for three professional references or three letters of recommendation. Additional materials, such as a teaching philosophy statement and transcripts, are optional but strongly encouraged. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Supply-Chain-Management_R-097482-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Supply Chain Management", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Supply Chain Management Agency Texas A&M University - Central Texas Department College of Business Administration Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Killeen, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Business Administration (COBA) at Texas A&M University-Central Texas welcomes highly qualified applicants to fill an immediate need for an Assistant Professor of Supply Chain Management starting in Fall 2027.\u00a0 This is a tenure-track faculty position.\u00a0 Application reviews will begin immediately.\u00a0 We are looking for a collegial teacher-scholar with a passion for teaching and a multi-faceted track record of excellence both within and beyond the classroom.\u00a0 Our greatest and immediate teaching need is for undergraduate courses in support of our brand-new BBA in Logistics & Supply Chain Management program. \u00a0Our hope is that this faculty member will help establish this as a strong program with great student outcomes and robust regional industry connections.\u00a0 Courses at other levels and in other related areas may also be available on a limited basis depending on applicant qualifications and interest.\u00a0 \u00a0 About Texas A&M University \u2013 Central Texas Established as an independent member of the Texas A&M University System in 2009, A&M-Central Texas is a friendly and dynamic regional teaching institution that prides itself on excellence in instruction but also embraces a growing emphasis on research.\u00a0 A&M-Central Texas is truly unique in that it is an upper- and masters-level institution, offering only junior- and senior-level coursework needed to successfully complete baccalaureate degrees and all coursework leading to the completion of master\u2019s degrees.\u00a0 As such, A&M-Central Texas maintains active partnerships with the major community colleges within the Greater Austin and Central Texas regions, as well as with Fort Hood, a premier outpost of the U.S. Army and one of the largest military installations in the world.\u00a0 Our multifaceted student demographic includes a significant proportion of first-generation college students, non-traditional learners, and military-affiliated personnel.\u00a0 \u00a0 The College of Business Administration is accredited by AACSB, and we are eager to have energetic and collegial new faculty members partner with us in pursuit of our major strategic initiatives, of which there are many on the near horizon (most notably, a DBA program anticipated to launch Fall 2027 pending SACSCOC final approval).\u00a0 This is an exciting time of rapid change within the University and College that affords new faculty members many opportunities to make an immediate, significant, and lasting impact. \u00a0 A&M-Central Texas is located on the southern edge of Killeen, TX, a city of approximately 150,000 located about halfway between Austin and Waco\u2014about 60 miles either way.\u00a0 Our faculty members enjoy a wide variety of living options by virtue of the range of communities in the area\u2014from quiet and rural to bustling and cosmopolitan.\u00a0 It is an easy drive to great art, food, shopping, and night life as well as to hunting, fishing, hiking, and camping for those who prefer the outdoors.\u00a0 Central Texas is a rapidly growing region with a booming economy, but is also a great place for families, with many options for schooling, worship, civic engagement, and recreation.\u00a0 It also has modest traffic and a reasonable cost of living. \u00a0The major metropolitan areas of Houston, Dallas-Fort Worth, and San Antonio are all within a 3-hour radius of Killeen.\u00a0 Responsibilities: The candidate will be expected to provide quality, engaging instruction for typically three courses per term, primarily at the undergraduate level and in a variety of course delivery formats (face-to-face, online, or hybrid), with fully online being the most in-demand option at present. \u00a0Candidates who possess exceptional skill at making technical content accessible to a broad audience are especially desired.\u00a0 The candidate will be expected to teach the following courses: LSCM 4321 Production and Operations Management, LSCM 4322 Business Process, Quality, and Lean Management, LSCM 4326 Global Procurement and Strategic Sourcing.\u00a0 Other assigned courses may include LSCM 4323 Supply Chain Management and BUSI 3311 Business Statistics.\u00a0 Additional summer teaching opportunities may be available depending on student demand and department needs.\u00a0 Some scholarly contributions are also required.\u00a0 The candidate is expected have sufficient scholarly and/or professional activities to have \u201cscholarly academic\u201d status upon arrival per AACSB faculty classifications, and to have a healthy pipeline of works in progress toward publication, where health is measured more by viability and anticipated impact than by number and/or status.\u00a0 Scholarship is but one category of currency and impact with which faculty may engage: others include maintaining a recognized professional certification, presenting at academic conferences, engaging in consulting or other industry-related activities, and completing other relevant professional training and development activities.\u00a0 Professional development funds are available to support all of these endeavors, and faculty within the College frequently collaborate on research projects together.\u00a0 \u00a0 In regard to service, faculty are expected to support their program(s), department, college, and/or university with committee work, but first-year faculty are exempt from this.\u00a0 In addition, faculty are expected to have some sort of service to their profession and/or to the community, but again, service contribution impact and quality are more important than the numbers of activities engaged in. \u00a0Faculty generally have a lot of discretion in determining how best they can add value through their various service activities.\u00a0 A Presidential Proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on all new H\u20111B petitions filed after September 21, 2025, and Texas A&M University\u2013Central Texas will not pay this fee. Additionally, a moratorium issued by Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026, restricts the filing of new H\u20111B petitions unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. Applicants must be authorized to work for any U.S. employer. Minimum Qualifications: To be eligible to apply for this position, candidates should: Possess a terminal degree (doctorate) in supply chain management or a closely related discipline from a regionally accredited university. Be eligible for the AACSB \u201cscholarly academic\u201d faculty classification (two publications or relevant terminal degree completed since 2022, with viable works in progress). Have a documented track record of successfully teaching supply chain or operations courses, including in fully online formats. Be qualified to teach LSCM 4321, LSCM 4322, and LSCM 4326. \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: The ideal candidate for this position would also possess: At least three (3) years of full-time collegiate teaching experience. Industry experience. Experience developing industry connections in support of academic programs. Proficiency in creating original and engaging online course instructional materials. Qualifications to teach LSCM 4323 and BUSI 3311. Great administrative, organizational, and interpersonal skills to support successful instruction to a largely non-traditional, first-generation, and military-affiliated student body. Familiarity/experience with DBA programs and/or supervision of doctoral students. Salary: Commensurate Hours: Faculty hours; M-F; hours may vary by assignment and course modality. To Apply: Please apply directly on our Texas A&M University-Central Texas Job Site . Applicants are required to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), and either the contact information for three professional references or three letters of recommendation. Additional materials, such as a teaching philosophy statement and transcripts, are optional but strongly encouraged. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Adjunct-Faculty---Criminal-Justice_R-057255": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Criminal Justice", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Faculty - Criminal Justice Agency Texas A&M University - Central Texas Department College Of Arts & Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Killeen, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Description of Job Responsibility/Duty: 100% - Teaches an undergraduate level class in criminal justice as needed.\u00a0 Writes syllabi for the courses to be taught using the approved format of the College of Arts and Sciences. \u00a0Meets with students enrolled in their classes when students need additional assistance with class material and assignments. Job Summary/Basic Function: Primarily responsible for the teaching/learning process.\u00a0 Adjunct instructors are hired to teach on a temporary and part-time basis. Adjunct instructors teaching courses for credit must meet the same requirements for professional and scholarly preparation as their full-time counterparts teaching in the same discipline. Minimum Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in Criminal Justice or related field and undergraduate teaching experience Preferred qualifications Ph.D. in Criminal Justice or related field Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Experience in teaching in criminal justice. Show expertise in and commitment to undergraduate criminal justice education. Exhibit enthusiasm for undergraduate teaching and employing innovative teaching methods. Required Applicant Documents: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Veterans/Disability Employer committed to diversity. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Adjunct-Faculty---Sociology_R-057035": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Sociology", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Faculty - Sociology Agency Texas A&M University - Central Texas Department College Of Arts & Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Killeen, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Applications for part-time adjunct faculty positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed when openings become available. Future teaching assignments are on a semester-by-semester basis, which may include fall, spring and summer.\u00a0 The Social Sciences Department at Texas A&M University-Central Texas is seeking applicants for a sociology adjunct instructor position. The successful candidate will be expected to teach an upper-level course in sociology. Areas of specialization are open, but we are especially interested in candidates who can teach at least one of the following topics: social inequalities, health and illness, media, political sociology, or the military. Experience and enthusiasm for teaching and working with undergraduate students is essential. Because demand for online courses is growing, candidates do not need to live in Central Texas. A Ph.D. in sociology is preferred.\u00a0 Please submit a curriculum vitae, transcripts, and a cover letter describing your fit for the position and whether you would be willing to teach online, face to face, or both.\u00a0 Job Summary: Primarily responsible for the teaching/learning process.\u00a0 Adjunct instructors are hired to teach on a temporary and part-time basis. Adjunct instructors teaching courses for credit must meet the same requirements for professional and scholarly preparation as their full-time counterparts teaching in the same discipline. Responsibilities : Teaches an undergraduate level class in sociology as needed.\u00a0 Writes syllabi for the courses to be taught using the approved format of the College of Arts and Sciences. Responds to student needs via email and with grading feedback in a timely manner.\u00a0 Meets with students enrolled in their classes when students need additional assistance with class material and assignments. Minimum Qualifications: Masters in sociology Experience in teaching in sociology. Show expertise in and commitment to undergraduate sociology education. Exhibit enthusiasm for undergraduate teaching and employing innovative teaching methods. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in Sociology or related field A Presidential Proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on all new H\u20111B petitions filed after September 21, 2025, and Texas A&M University\u2013Central Texas will not pay this fee. Additionally, a moratorium issued by Governor Abbott on January 27, 2026, restricts the filing of new H\u20111B petitions unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Due to these restrictions, applicants must be authorized to work for any U.S. employer, and the department is currently unable to sponsor or assume sponsorship of any employment visa. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Adjunct-Faculty---Psychology_R-082450": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Psychology", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-28\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Faculty - Psychology Agency Texas A&M University - Central Texas Department College Of Education and Human Development Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Killeen, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Applications for part-time adjunct faculty positions are accepted on a continuous basis and reviewed when openings become available. Future teaching assignments are on a semester-by-semester basis, which may include fall, spring and summer.\u00a0 The College of Education and Human Development\u2019s Department of Counseling and Psychology is seeking an adjunct to contribute to our goal of accessible, affordable, and quality education as well as our core values of integrity, innovation, creativity, excellence, caring support, and community connection. Applicants must be authorized to work for any US employer. The department is unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa at this time. Job Summary: The faculty member will teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Psychology. Additional responsibilities may include student academic advising, engaging in university events, and conducting research and scholarship activities.\u00a0\u00a0 Minimum Requirements: A Master\u2019s degree in Psychology or a closely related field is required for undergraduate courses, and a Doctorate degree is required for graduate courses. Both degrees must be approved by the university and recognized by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools. Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. approved by the university and recognized by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools as appropriate to Psychology or a closely related field. Teaching experience at the undergraduate and/or graduate level that includes active engagement of students in the learning process. Experience teaching online courses that include integration of research-based practices in online course design and delivery Additional Qualifications: Ability in the discipline and clear promise of teaching excellence as evidenced in evaluation by peers, department head, and college dean. A record of scholarly activity beyond that required for completion of the terminal degree. Must possess the minimum credential standards of the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools (SACSCOC), which include at least 18 graduate semester credit hours in the subject area of suitable approved justifications. Effective communicator who can collaborate with a multifaceted group of stakeholders. Required Applicant Documents: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Graduate Transcripts Teaching Philosophy 3 Professional References All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/CIS-Adjunct-Faculty_R-086088": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - CIS", "description": "Posted: 2025-10-31\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Faculty - CIS Agency Texas A&M University - Central Texas Department College Of Business Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Killeen, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Subhani Department of Computer Information Systems at Texas A&M University\u2013Central Texas is seeking applicants for Spring and/or Summer 2026 adjunct instructor positions.\u00a0Successful candidates will be expected to teach one or more of the courses in programming, data communications, computer networking, database management, cybersecurity, and other related areas in computer information systems or Computer Science as determined by department needs and individual qualifications. Enthusiasm for teaching and working with undergraduate students is essential. A master\u2019s degree in information systems or computer science or a related field is required. This is an open-ended search and applications will be taken at any time. Applicants must be authorized to work for any US employer. The department is unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa at this time. Job Summary: Primarily responsible for the teaching/learning process.\u00a0 Adjunct instructors are hired to teach on a temporary and part-time basis Job Responsibility/Duty: Teaches undergraduate-level classes in the Computer Information Systems program as needed.\u00a0 Writes syllabi for the courses to be taught using the approved format of the College of Business Administration.\u00a0 Meets with students enrolled in their classes when students need additional assistance with class material and assignments. Minimum qualifications : Master\u2019s degree in information systems or computer science or related field. Preferred qualifications : Earned Doctorate in Information Systems / Computer Science or a closely related degree/area. Significant industry experience in the areas listed above or Industry-recognized technical certifications. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Demonstrated experience or expertise in teaching, particularly at the undergraduate level, with a focus on student engagement and academic success. Proven expertise in Computer Information Systems or Computer Science and a strong commitment to high-quality undergraduate education. Required Applicant Documents: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Undergraduate Transcripts Graduate Transcripts To Apply: Please apply directly on our Texas A&M University-Central Texas Job Site . Please submit a cover letter, a resume, transcripts, and the contact information of three professional references when applying for this position. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Adjunct-Faculty---Clinical-Mental-Health-Counseling_R-074692": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Clinical Mental Health Counseling", "description": "Posted: 2025-04-10\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Faculty - Clinical Mental Health Counseling Agency Texas A&M University - Central Texas Department College Of Education and Human Development Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Killeen, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Education and Human Development\u2019s Department of Counseling and Psychology is seeking an adjunct to contribute to our goal of accessible, affordable, and quality education as well as our core values of excellence and achievement, compassion, integrity, knowledge, respect for all, initiative, and collaboration. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution\u2019s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution\u2019s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."}}, "rows": {"https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Access-Services-Librarian---Faculty_R-097876": {"school_id": 1406, "posting_url": "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Access-Services-Librarian---Faculty_R-097876", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Librarian, Access Services", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-10-09", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Management-Strategy_R-097888-1": {"school_id": 1406, "posting_url": "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Management-Strategy_R-097888-1", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor of Management/Strategy", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of Business Administration", "area_key_words": "Management/Strategy", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-10-09"}, "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUCT_External/job/Killeen-TX/Adjunct-Faculty---Marriage---Family-Therapy_R-083523-1": {"school_id": 1406, "posting_url"